# file: internal/server/testdata/write_op_modes.golden
# version: 1.26.0
# guid: 656b77a9-3e50-456c-9945-dbbebbd7e041
# last-edited: 2026-10-26
#
# What `{}` does for every registered operation that can write (declares
# library.write, files.write or db.migrate, declares the resources it writes
# (OperationDef.Writes), or declares no capabilities at all).
# Read by internal/server/write_op_modes_test.go
# (TestWriteOps_EveryWriteOpHasARecordedMode): every such op must have exactly
# one line here, and every line must name a registered op.
#
# /api/v3/ops does not read this file. `preview` here says only that an
# omitted mode writes nothing; it does not say which params key the op reads
# (several gate on apply or live, not dry_run, and a few preview only through
# a different op). How an op previews in v3 is the op's own declaration,
# OperationDef.Preview, checked against its params type by
# TestOpsV3_PreviewDeclarationsMatchTheOpsParams
# (internal/server/wire_ops_v3_routes_test.go). That test also requires every
# op listed `preview` here to declare a Preview (the params type its Run
# decodes; every mode key in it is written) or to be listed in its
# previewOnlyElsewhere table with the reason, and every `no-mode` op to
# declare none.
#
# Classes:
#   preview  omitted mode is a preview (owner rule 2026-09-25)
#   no-mode  the op has no preview mode at all; it always runs for real.
#            Known gap, docs/audits/2026-09-25-op-preview-default-inventory.md
#            section 5. Do NOT add a new op here to make the test pass: give it
#            a preview mode (opmode.ResolveDryRun) and list it as preview.
#
# There is no "live" class on purpose. A writing op whose omitted mode is live
# violates the owner rule; it gets a preview mode, not a ledger entry.
#
# Maintenance-job ops (maintenance.<job id> from internal/maintenance/jobs) are
# not listed: TestMaintenanceJobs_PreviewByDefault checks their advertised
# default against the job registry directly.
#
# Seeded 2026-09-25 from the inventory doc's sections 1-5.
#
# 2026-10-18 (05-PR9): six ops that wrote while declaring only read
# capabilities were found by a sweep of every op /api/v3/ops treated as
# read-only. They now declare their write capability and are listed here:
# itunes.playlist-import, maintenance.cover-text-read and
# maintenance.file-provenance-export already previewed by default;
# deluge.path-update, maintenance.regroup-shattered-ai and the full-transcribe
# path of maintenance.transcribe-book-intros got a dry_run preview mode
# (omitted = preview) rather than a no-mode line.

